195 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 129 0 R
/E (The near-term opportunity set in the Gulf has tilted from growth-and-attraction toward resilience. Bypass and routing infrastructure, storage, energy-security assets, air defence, and monetisation structures of the KPC type are where capital and deal flow are concentrating, and where sovereign and private co-investment is most available. Exposure built purely on the pre-war expansion narrative, in tourism, hospitality, and giga-project supply chains, now carries visibly more risk and a longer recovery path with contingencies.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
